BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Ride Day 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T210000
DTSTAMP:20260805T080600Z
UID:06d74b8d-c48d-5239-b783-beb17f155db9
DESCRIPTION:Hamilton Bike Share is excited to present our inaugural FREE R
 IDE DAY\, brought to you by Cogeco. Free Ride Day is coming your way on Su
 nday\, June 7th from 9 AM - 9 PM\, where you can ride for up to 3 hours on
  us\, using any Hamilton Bike Share bike in our service area with an exist
 ing HBS account.\n\nHow to Ride Free on June 7th:\n\n* Sign in to your exi
 sting account OR create a new Pay As You Go account in the Social Bicycles
  app. You will need a valid email and credit card to register. Select the 
 $0 prefill option if you do not wish to add any additional credit.\n\n* Us
 e the in-app map to find a bike near you. To unlock a bike\, scan the QR c
 ode at the back of the bike and remove the U-Bar. Remember to always bring
  the U-Bar with you! Store it securely in the holster slot parallel to the
  rear wheel.\n\n* Ride for up to 3 hours in one trip or across multiple sm
 aller trips between 9 AM - 9 PM on Sunday\, June 7th.\n\n* To end your tri
 p\, use the U-Bar to lock your bike to any Bike Share hub for free\, or lo
 ck to a public post or bike rack for a $1 convenience fee.\n\nAll our regu
 lar operating rules and fees for additional features\, like out of hub loc
 king and multi-bike rentals\, continue to apply! Stay in our service area 
 (between Dundas and Kenilworth Ave in the lower city) and never leave a bi
 ke unlocked and unattended. Always ensure bikes are locked to secure fixed
  objects when making a stop.\n\nNeed help? Contact us:\n\n(/cdn-cgi/l/emai
 l-protection#d2bab7bea292bab3bfbbbea6bdbcb0bbb9b7a1bab3a0b7fcb1b3) [email 
 protected]\n\n289-768-2453\nURL: https://www.everyonerides.org/free_ride_d
 ay_2026
LOCATION:See post
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/free_ride_day_2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mural Ride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T120000
DTSTAMP:20260805T080600Z
UID:90e2091d-efe1-5bcd-ad66-92db91dbb3f9
DESCRIPTION:Our Annual Mural Ride is SO back and this time with a sweet su
 rprise from one of our sponsors\, Cogeco! ☀️🍦🚲\n\nJoin us on Sat
 urday\, August 8th at 10am for a slow roll from Corktown Park down to our 
 Discovery Drive Hub at Pier 8. Along our ride we'll guide you through a cu
 rated route to check out some of the outstanding street and mural art we a
 re so lucky to have here in #HamOnt. We will take time along the route to 
 snap photos and share some knowledge and insights behind some of the artis
 ts and artwork featured along our way.\n\nWe are looking forward to a swee
 t end to the ride down at our Discovery Drive Hub where we will join up wi
 th our sponsors Cogeco who will be hosting a special pop-up activation. Th
 ey'll be handing out exclusive HBS t-shirts\, vouchers for free ice cream 
 at Waterfront Scoops\, and other fun goodies! Celebrate that post ride fee
 ling in the best way possible with fun merch\, sweet treats\, the waterfro
 nt and games 🌊⛱️ you don't want to miss this!\nURL: https://www.eve
 ryonerides.org/mural_ride_2026
LOCATION:Cork Town Bike Share Hub\, Ferguson Avenue and Young St\, Hamilto
 n\, ON\, ON L8N 2M8\, Canada
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/mural_ride_2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eco-Ride Series with Environment Hamilton
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T203000
DTSTAMP:20260805T080601Z
UID:a38e4242-6899-57f1-8bb1-6afbdaffe7e3
DESCRIPTION:When you ride a bike\, do you notice your environment more? Ar
 e you curious about the ecological story of Hamilton? We're launching a sp
 ecial Group Ride series in partnership with Environment Hamilton this summ
 er. Each ride will focus on a particular layer of environmentalism in the 
 context of our city\, with routes and teaching oriented toward a specific 
 theme. It's a great way to learn more about Hamilton's unique ecological h
 istory and challenges\, all from the seat of a bicycle.\n\nJoin us for the
  following two rides:\n\n🌳🏙️\n\nPark to Park\n\nOn Tuesday July 28
  Environment Hamilton and Hamilton Bike Share are hosting a Park to Park B
 ike Tour leaving from the Beasley Park Bike Share Hub. The ride will be ju
 st over 10 km with stops at four different parks and will end by 8pm. In a
 ddition to Beasley Park\, riders will stop at Dundurn Castle\, Churchill P
 ark\, Victoria Park\, and will discuss green space access as it relates to
  demographics in different areas of the city.\n\n📆Tuesday\, July 28\n\n
 ⏰6:30PM-8:00PM\n\n📍Beasley Park Bike Share Hub (Elgin St at Cannon St
  E)\n\nIndustrial Impacts\, Past & Present\n\nOn Thursday August 20\, Envi
 ronment Hamilton and Hamilton Bike Share are hosting an Industrial Impacts
  Past & Present Cycling Tour leaving from the Bayfront Park Bike Share Hub
 . The ride will be just over 10 km with stops and will end by 8pm. Cycling
  tour leads will discuss the impacts of industry\, legacy pollution\, and 
 waste dumping.\n\n📆Thursday\, August 20\n\n⏰6:30pm - 8:00pm\n\n📍Ba
 yfront Park bike share hub (Bay St N at Strachan St W under the Waterfront
  Trail sail post)\nURL: https://www.everyonerides.org/eco_ride_series
LOCATION:See post
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/eco_ride_series
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Valley Park Seasonal Hub Launch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T193000
DTSTAMP:20260805T080600Z
UID:ab36ac79-08aa-56e2-b2cd-005b08c5c01f
DESCRIPTION:🚨PSA for tonight's event!🚨\nDue to smoke/air quality thi
 s afternoon\, our Valley Park Launch Event is moving inside the rec centre
 . Join us inside to beat the heat and chat about our new pilot expansion w
 ith some delicious goodies. Here's hoping the air clears and we can enjoy 
 a ride soon!\n\n---\n\nWe're excited to share our new seasonal pilot progr
 am for Summer 2026: Bike Share at Valley Park!\n\nFor the months of July a
 nd August\, you can find a Bike Share Hub in the rec centre parking lot at
  Valley Park and enjoy a bike ride on the many beautiful trails there.\n\n
 Join us for our launch event and enjoy some delicious baked goods while mi
 ngling with your neighbours from the City of Hamilton and Ward 9!\n\nWe'd 
 like to extend our thanks to Councillor Brad Clark and the leadership of W
 ard 9 for partnering with us on this exciting project. See you at the park
 !\n\n📆 Wednesday\, July 15th\n\n⏰6:30PM-7:30PM\n\n📍Hamilton Bike S
 hare Hub @ Valley Park parking lot\nURL: https://www.everyonerides.org/val
 ley_park
LOCATION:See post
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/valley_park
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
